2 CONT
2 CONT (From the writing of his older brother Chén Mó 陳謨:)[GC] My third younger brother, Yëin, is a senior councillor in Gōng Xäi 廣西 (Guǎngxī) Province. He had four sons: Fāt, Fūk, Siù, and Wμ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fāt was appointed as a district magistrate in Liũ Jiü 柳州 (Liǔzhōu) [a city in 廣西 (Guǎngxī) Province] with the title of Fifteenth Lõng 郎 [Láng]. He had three sons: Gïm Sän, Yẽng Sän, and Fō Sän. ( Gïm Sän sons relocation:)[GC]
2 CONT * Xü Màng 師孟 lived in Sèng Jàk Bāk Lùt 上澤北律 (Shàngzéběilǜ).
2 CONT * Xü Jùng 師仲 lived in Bàk Sêk Gëin Hēo Ü Hùk Lão Suī Tûn 白石逕口都斛澇水村 (Báishíjìngkǒudoūhúlàoshuǐcūn).
2 CONT * Xü Lèng 師亮 lived in Üng Hâng Bàk Sêk Füng Göng Chüng Gïm Tûn 東坑白石豐江沖金村 (Dōngkēngbáishífēngjiāngchōngjīncūn).
2 CONT * Xü Lī 師李 lived in Kĩ Fũng Dū Lêng Bü Hâng Tún Xïn Vòi Vãng Pū 奇逢子領布坑村新會橫浦 (Qíféngzílĩngbùkēngcūnxīnhuìhéngpǔ).
2 CONT
2 CONT (This must be Fūk's son 富山)[GC] Fù 富 moved to Chẽl Yẽng 朝陽 (Cháoyáng) and lived in Gëin Pöi Vōng Chüng 逕背汪沖 (Jìngbèiwāngchüng).
2 CONT
2 CONT (His 4th son 壽 Shòu has two sons: 年 Nián and 養Yàng)[GC]
2 CONT * Yàng 養 lived in Lũng Suī Vōng Chüng Tûn 瀧水汪沖村 (Lóngshuǐwāngchüngcūn). 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Clarification by George Chin 7/25/2011]
2 CONT
2 CONT Translated from: Chen Hui's third son 英 Ying in the 陈氏宗亲网 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.chens.org.cn/shownews.asp?newsid=1438
2 CONT
2 CONT The village 玉怀(懷) Yùhuái in 台山 Taishan descended from 英 Yīng. 英 Yīng had four sons: 法福寿(壽)悟 Fǎ, Fú, Shòu, and Wù. 寿(壽) Shòu has two sons: 年 Nián and 養Yàng. So far this is the same as I have on the Huang Village Chin Family Tree si
2 CONC te http://www3.fitnyc.edu/gene_chin/tree. You can also find 玉怀(懷) Yùhuái  village in my larger Taishan map. It is southeast of 三合 Sanhe. Then it continues with 年 Nián's descendents. 年 Nián's son was 华(華)清 Huáqīng. 华(華)清 Huáqīng's 
2 CONC descendents (doesn't say sons or grandsons, or later) are 闰(閏)长(長) Rùnzhǎng, 癸长(長) Guǐzhǎng, 亚(亞)长(長) Yàzhǎng, and 闰(閏)福 Rùnfú. Some generations later they had 碧崖 Bìyá and 雲崖 Yúnyá. Still more generations later there was a 可大 Kědà
2 CONC  who moved to 玉怀(懷) Yùhuái village. Then they had a 泰翁 Tàiwēng. He must be a very important person but no details on his descendents or who he was. It has other detail on how some of the people died and they mourned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants next 3 to 4 generations taken from :
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.chens.org.cn/shownews.asp?newsid=1194
