1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lunar birthdate: 宋哲宗元祐元年5月23日 遼道宗大安2年5月23日　 Birthdate converted from lunar to solar: July 6, 1086 (Monday) Lunar repose date: 宋孝宗淳熙10年7月14日 金世宗大定23年7月14日　 Repose date converted from lunar to solar: August 3, 1183 (
2 CONC Wednesday)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Chin Family Tree of Foo Chung Village of Chung Shan District of Kwong Tung Province China. 《廣東中山縣庫充鄉陳氏族譜》 (Harry Lin Chin Foundation Vancouver, BC, 1980), pg. 20-22
2 CONT
2 CONT  Tien Kuo was originally named Yuen Ying元英and was also known as Hong Shou香叟，He begot 3 sons and a daughter。（The daughter was married to Mar Nan-Pao馬南保of Sar-Chung沙涌）。Tien Kuo was originally a resident of Hui-lou奎漏，Chu-Chi Lane珠磯巷i
2 CONC n Pao-Chang County保昌縣of Nan-Hsiung Prefecture南雄府，and in the eighth year of Sue Hing紹興0f Sung Dynasty宋朝（1138）。He took the test of Po-Shuye-科學Jong-Chee進士（a honor for exceedingly well informed man）and was granted Chin-進Shih士（a Degree
2 CONC  equivalent to a PHD）。In the year of Yen-Wu壬午年（1162），he tooki the position as an imperial counsellor。But for his loyalit y and straight-forward language，he was sent to Wen-Shun Village，文順鄉Tung-Gon County東莞縣in Canton廣東省，There he re
2 CONC sided in a fortress，He was then the governor over those fortresses and was responsible for the safety of the people there。He managed to have three hundred and ninety seven hectres，and sixty-six acres of farming land; and harvested
2 CONC  one thousand two hundred and seventy-eight picul of autumn rice among which one thousand piculs were enough to spend on military supply。The remaining two hundred and  seventy-eight piculs were  changed for money to pay for the Tu
2 CONC ng-Guan東莞fortress. They proposed to build fortresses there because sea pirates attacked there frequently，For the convenience of commercial exchange，the local residents（the Cheng's鄭氏）wanted to
2 CONT
2 CONT -21-
2 CONT
2 CONT have the fortified town at Yung-Mark雍陌，My ancestor，Tien Kuo，did not wish to argue, and said only that heavy soil was valuable and suitable for the establishment of a fortified town，Then he secretly refined the ferrous sand by mixi
2 CONC no it with the soil Naturally the soil was heavier than Yung-Mark The argument was settled and Ching-Shan青山（IronTown鐵城）was actualized，In the twenty-second year of Shao-Hing紹興（1152），he contributed several thousand of ten-pecks，As a
2 CONC  result，Hong-Shan香山town，established，In the twenty-sixth year of Shao-Hing紹興（1156），he  contributed again for the establishment of an institute college at Lien-Fung蓮率山（Lotus Mountain）.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tien Kuo was born on the twenty-third day of May of fored rid so 081 toll。the first year of Yuen-Yen（1086），and died on the 14th day of July of the eighth year of Tsuen-Shih（1182）at the age of ninety-six。His wife（Miss Lo羅氏）was born
2 CONC  on the third day of February on the 4th year of Yuen-Yew（1094），and died on the 16th day of August of the 10th year of Tsuen-Shih（1188）at the age of 94. The couple were jointly buried at the How- Shan後門山of Fo0- Ching庫充鄉Village。The
2 CONC  tombs were seated on the east hill，facing the west and also received the protection earthly guardian gods.
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION（三世） 彥晏公（YENMUN）生二子：姚卿公（YUEHING），振卿公 FOURTH GENERATION（四世） 姚卿公（YUEHING）生一子：桂芳公（GAIFONG）。
2 CONT
