2 CONT 必恩 Bēik Yïn (Bì’ēn) was the second son of 應隆 Yëin Lũng. His tomb was in Jüng Xïm Pẽin 中心坪 (Zhōngxīnpíng) in the shape of a snake. He married a woman from the M 吳 (Wú) family. Her tomb was in Yïn Pẽin Sïm Hǎng 恩平深坑 (Ēnpíngshēnkēng)
2 CONC  in the shape of a person facing ENE 3/4N or 60 degrees. They had two sons: 斗秀 Ēo Xiü and 斗祥 Ēo Tẽng. 
