2 NOTE Ken,
3 CONT
3 CONT I suggest the title for your maternal pedigree chart to read as “Guangdong First Ancestor Chen Fengtai to Chen Zhao Fan (Chin Sui Fan) Descendants in US” (廣東始祖陳鳳臺至美國陳肇蕃裔).
3 CONT
3 CONT The dates of birth and death for your maternal ancestors are provided in your Jiapu. I normally would indicate the year of birth and death of each ancestor at sides of the chart.  If you wish to include them, I suppose you are abl
3 CONC e to convert the dates given therein into Gregorian dates. If you can do that, it would save me sometime in extracting the information from the related profiles in your jiapu to convert them.
3 CONT
3 CONT There are interesting commentaries and/or family histories for some of your maternal ancestors provided in the jiapu. If you can get them translated, it would be interesting to include them as well.
3 CONT
3 CONT If the generation names are given in the jiapu, you may wish to include them as well.  If it is in the form of a poem, you could get it translated and include it and the translation into the chart.
3 CONT
3 CONT You may have family photos than you may wish to include them in the chart.
3 CONT
3 CONT If you know the movements of your ancestors from one place to another you may wish to provide a map showing such movements and indicating the generations that stayed in each place.   
3 CONT
3 CONT From maternal side you would be my 50th cousin 7 times removed.  The common ancestor is Jīn Gōng (Kuāng)[ 津公(匡)] at Generation  94,86,53,6.
3 CONT
3 CONT Philip
